---
description: Require user control over app launches, services, builds, and runtime processes
alwaysApply: true
---

# Manual Runtime Control

- Never start or restart the application, Expo, Metro, simulators, emulators,
  Docker services, API servers, databases, or other long-running processes.
- Never run build, bundle, export, archive, native compile, or deployment
  commands unless the user explicitly requests that exact action.
- Never stop, kill, or otherwise manipulate processes started by the user.
- After code changes, provide the exact command the user can run manually.
- Ask the user for logs or screenshots when runtime verification is needed.
- Static checks such as TypeScript, lint, and Expo Doctor are allowed unless
  the user also asks not to run them.
